 "structural_vcf_sha256": "dfb2d2ca36a98da441c705449ac48f7c703b0651b536e992c33efd7026b2419a",
 "structural_input": "35 synthetic structural and large-deletion records over chromosome 21, the coding-only-structural set's input: a deletion, a duplication and an inversion covering one protein-coding transcript whole, a deletion over one coding exon with intronic ends, a deletion inside an intron, a deletion of 70 bases over the same coding exon, a deletion from the coding sequence into an intron, a deletion from the 5' untranslated exon segment across the whole coding sequence into the 3' untranslated one, a deletion from the 3' untranslated exon segment over the stop codon into an intron, a deletion at an intergenic locus, and a 2 kb deletion centred on 25 of the corpus's loci; the reference allele is a placeholder (N, or A for one deletion), so the records run without a FASTA. The set compares under --coding_only alone: the pruned cache carries every transcript a record overlaps but not every transcript within the flanking distance of one, and the filter drops those upstream and downstream rows on both sides"
}
